#### <i>As of the writing of this module, **Claude** is the only LLM on this list that requires you to create an account.</i>

<br>

#### **2. Choose a topic.** It can be anything you wish to explore, such as:

* #### *How do I make a taco?*
* #### *What is the environmental impact of AI technology?*
* #### *How is AI being integrated into everyday technology?*
* #### *What materials do I need to make the best pillow fort?*

<br>

#### **3. Try a simple prompt**. Start with something open-ended such as:

<div style="width:80%; margin:0 auto 18px auto;">
  <div style="background:#F7F8FA; border-left:5px solid #8C52BA; border-radius:14px; padding:18px;">
    <div style="font-size:16px;">
      How do you make the best pillow fort?
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<br>

#### **4. Add detail.** For example, you can add some context and a tone to your prompt:


<div style="width:80%; margin:0 auto 18px auto;">
  <div style="background:#F7F8FA; border-left:5px solid #8C52BA; border-radius:14px; padding:18px;">
    <div style="font-size:16px;">
      Using fun and silly language, describe the materials needed to make the best pillow fort. Assume that the builders have access to supplies that might generally be found in a three bedroom house in Vermont.
    </div>
  </div>
</div>


#### You don't have to, but you may choose to use the TaCo FoRT prompting structure. 

<p align="center">
<img src="https://images.code.org/a9b6ae8f94bfa64afbf2af4a60ec6609-Screenshot 2025-04-07 at 2.01.43 PM.png" alt="lesson plan diagram" width="70%" style="border-radius:10px; border: 5px solid black;">
</p>

<br>

#### **5. Keep exploring.** Continue to practice prompting. Explore with different prompting techniques, amount of detail, or even try multimodal prompting.

<div style="width:80%; margin:0 auto 18px auto;">
  <div style="background:#F7F8FA; border-left:5px solid #8C52BA; border-radius:14px; padding:18px;">
    <div style="font-size:16px;">
      Give me an image of the ultimate pillow fort. Make it as warm and cozy as possible.
    </div>
  </div>
</div>


<br>

#### **6. Take it further.** If you have time, try prompting in two or more LLMs to see how the responses differ.

<br>

>#### **💬 Quick Reflection:** How successful where different prompting techniques? What were some aspects of a good prompt? What were some aspects of a bad prompt?

